CORE
main.c
--paths lifo
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
This test pins down the `--paths`-friendliness of the CPROVER library's `free`
and `__CPROVER_deallocate`: the bookkeeping in those two functions emits GOTO
branches that, under `--paths lifo`, multiplied the symex state space
exponentially with the number of `free` calls. With if-conversion turning
those branches into conditional assignments, this test runs in a handful of
paths instead of 4^N. Without if-conversion it would time out at the harness
limit, so a regression is observable here.
